{% icon id="sinking-ship" size=32 /%}Sailing for {% term id="aquamarine" %}aquamarine{% /term %}? The Storms {% term id="module" %}module{% /term %} attacks the {% term id="fortress" %}fortresses{% /term %} of the {% term id="storm-islands" %}Storm Islands{% /term %}, and it keeps your Storm Islands castle supplied with {% term id="mead" %}mead{% /term %}. It has two tabs: **Attack Storm Fortresses** and **Mead replace**.

{% terms_on_page /%}

You need the Storm Islands unlocked in the game and a castle there.

## Attack Storm Fortresses {% #attack %}

This tab attacks the fortresses around your Storm Islands castle.

1. The bot reads the map around your Storm Islands castle and lists the fortresses. If you allowed [gge-tracker.com timetables](/war-room/dashboard/#gge-tracker), it takes the fortresses and their times from the site instead, also the ones the map does not show yet, and still checks each one in the game before it attacks.
2. It puts them in **Fort order**. **Highest level first** tries the highest level and the fewest hits left first, nearest first among equals. **Nearest first** goes by distance alone.
3. It skips fortresses whose level you did not tick, fortresses that are still waiting, and fortresses one of your armies is marching to.
4. It takes a free {% term id="commander-game" %}commander{% /term %}. If you picked an order on the {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.title" /%} card, it follows it. Otherwise it takes the free commander with the best loot bonus.
5. When every fortress is waiting, the bot waits for the next one, then goes on.

The fortress levels are two groups of switches. Under **Easy fortresses**, levels 60, 70 and 80 are on by default. Under **Hard fortresses**, levels 40 to 80 are off by default. If you turn every level off, the bot uses easy 60, 70 and 80 and hard 70 and 80.

This tab is an attack {% term id="plugin" %}plugin{% /term %}, so it counts toward your {% term id="attack-cap" %}attack cap{% /term %}. **Mead replace** does not.

## Army: Autofill or Waves {% #army %}

{% ui key="client:army.mode.autofill" /%} sends 3 {% term id="wave" %}waves{% /term %}. It puts troops on the left and right {% term id="flank" %}flanks{% /term %} of each wave, and wall {% term id="tool" %}tools{% /term %} on the left flank of the first wave. It waits until the castle holds at least 100 troops.

{% ui key="client:army.mode.waves" /%} sends exactly the waves you write, or a [virtual preset](/modules/virtual-presets/).

For the horse, **Use fast horse feathers** spends one {% term id="horse-feather" %}feather{% /term %} on each attack, and the troops go without one when you have none. **Use a coin horse** needs a stable in the castle.

## Spend aquamarine {% #aquamarine %}

When your aquamarine store is within 100,000 of full, the bot spends the aquamarine above **Aquamarine to keep** in the Storm Islands shop. It buys in this order, as far as the aquamarine goes:

1. **Buy coins**, which is on by default. One package costs 75,000 aquamarine.
2. The **Decoration** you pick. Crab Rock and Tide Garden cost 75,000. Whale Lagoon costs 100,000.
3. **Buy 5-hour skips** and **Buy 24-hour skips**. Each package costs 40,000. The bot never buys more packages in one session than the shop sells.
4. **Buy XP**. One package costs 10,000.
5. **Buy mock peasants**, 5 for 1,570. This spends what the choices above leave.

## Keep tools in stock {% #tool-stock %}

Under **Tools to keep in stock**, set **Scaling ladders**, **Battering rams** and **Mantlets**. When the Storm Islands castle holds fewer than that, the bot buys 1,000 from the armourer with coins. A value of 0 buys nothing.

The bot checks about every 30 minutes. **Most coins spent on them in one check** caps one check, and **Coins to keep** is the least you keep.

## Send wood and stone {% #resource-send %}

Turn on **Send wood and stone from the Storm Islands to your other castles**. When the bot starts, and then every 30 minutes, it sends the Storm Islands castle's wood and stone to your {% term id="main-castle" %}main castle{% /term %} and your {% term id="kingdom" %}kingdom{% /term %} castles, as much as each one has room for. It sends nothing to {% term id="berimond" %}Berimond{% /term %}.

## Mead replace {% #mead-replace %}

The **Mead replace** tab sends mead from your main castle in the {% term id="great-empire" %}Great Empire{% /term %} to your Storm Islands castle, so the mead there does not run out.

1. The bot works out how many hours of mead the Storm Islands castle has left.
2. When that drops below **Send mead when it lasts less than**, it sends mead to fill the castle.
3. If **Mead the main castle keeps** is above 0, it sends only the mead your main castle holds beyond that amount.
4. If a mead shipment on its way would land too late, the bot may spend a {% term id="time-skip" %}time skip{% /term %} on it.
5. After each shipment, it checks again about 15 minutes later.

If the Storm Islands castle can't store mead for more than about 3 hours, the {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} warns you that your mead may run out and you could lose troops.

## Test with Log only {% #log-only %}

Turn on **Log only: write the attacks to the log instead of sending them** on the attack tab. The bot builds each attack and each shop order and writes it to the log, but sends nothing to the game.

